course: dictionary
lesson: 625
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word baby has more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one you need. A baby can be a very young child who cannot yet walk or talk much, or a very young animal, like «a baby bird».
explain: Baby can also be an adjective, a word that describes a noun. In «baby carrots» and «baby teeth», baby means very small or young. Ask yourself: is the word naming a thing, or telling you what the thing is like?
explain: Context also tells you what babies need. Living things grow from babies to adults, and babies need care, gentle handling and help from an adult. Never shake a baby.
fact: A baby is a very young child who cannot yet walk or talk much.
fact: A baby can also be a very young animal, such as «a baby panda».
fact: «Baby» can be an adjective meaning very small or young, as in «baby teeth».
fact: Baby teeth sit in the mouth first, and the grown-up teeth wait underneath them until it is time for them to come through.
fact: Babies need gentle handling and help from an adult; never shake a baby.
exercise: «Picture a dentist's X-ray of a seven-year-old: the baby teeth sit in the mouth.» In this sentence, what are baby teeth? | *The first teeth a child has, which later fall out | Teeth that never fall out | Teeth that are very big and strong | Teeth made from plastic
exercise: In «a baby bird», what does baby mean? | A very small toy bird | The youngest person in a family | A grown-up bird that cannot fly | *A very young animal
exercise: In «baby carrots», what kind of word is baby? | Noun, the name of a thing | Adverb, it tells how something is done | Verb, it shows an action | *Adjective, it describes the carrots
test: «A newborn baby has more bones than an adult.» Why is this true? | *Some bones join together as we grow | Adults grow extra bones every day | Babies are heavier than adults | Babies eat more food than adults
test: «Ella is the baby of her family.» What does baby mean here? | A small adjective describing Ella | A very young animal | A child who is always crying | *The youngest person in a family
exam: In «Animal stories are some of the most shared news in the world: a baby panda, a shark in a flooded street, a clever crow, orcas pushing boats», which example is a very young animal? | a clever crow | *a baby panda | a shark in a flooded street | orcas pushing boats
